    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Nextdoor’s neighborhood platform is showing renewed operational momentum, with a sequential jump in weekly active users signaling improving engagement after a period of stagnation. The advertising-driven business is benefiting from a modest recovery in demand, pushing revenue growth ahead of internal expectations. Efficiency gains are visible, as the company nears breakeven adjusted EBITDA, reflecting tighter cost control even as it continues to invest in the community network. The core domestic market remains the focus, and no material geographic or regulatory disruptions are cited, though year-over-year user growth is still tepid.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership delivered a clean beat-and-raise quarter, surprising the market with near-breakeven results and moving the profitability timeline forward. The board immediately authorized a share repurchase program, signaling confidence in the intrinsic value and an intention to offset dilution. However, insider trading data paints a less enthusiastic picture: all recorded transactions in the past six months are officer sales, with no open-market purchases. This pattern tempers the buyback’s positive signal, suggesting that while public narrative emphasizes an accelerating path to profitability, some internal stakeholders are reducing exposure.",
